---
layout: base.njk
title: Devices
description: MIDI controllers gemifi runs on, is being ported to, or has been researched for — with an honest status for each.
permalink: /devices/
---
<section class="hero">
  <h1>Devices</h1>
  <p>Where gemifi runs today, what's in progress, and what we've only studied so far.</p>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <ul class="card-grid device-grid">
    {% for d in collections.devices %}
    <li>
      <article class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">{{ d.data.maker }}</p>
        <h3><a class="card-link" href="{{ d.url | url }}">{{ d.data.model }}</a></h3>
        <p>{{ d.data.summary }}</p>
        <div class="card-foot">
          <span class="status status-{{ d.data.status }}">{{ statuses[d.data.status].label }}</span>
        </div>
      </article>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <h2>What the statuses mean</h2>
  <dl class="facts legend">
    {% for key, st in statuses %}
    <div>
      <dt><span class="status status-{{ key }}">{{ st.label }}</span></dt>
      <dd>{{ st.description }}</dd>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </dl>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <h2>Add a device</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Each device is one Markdown file in
      <a href="{{ site.tree }}site/src/devices" rel="noopener"><code>site/src/devices/</code></a>.
      Copy the closest one, change its front matter (maker, model, status, the
      facts table, the device YAML) and rewrite the sections below it. The
      device list and its page build themselves from that file.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you've got gemifi running on something new, the device YAML goes in
      <a href="{{ site.tree }}devices" rel="noopener"><code>devices/</code></a>.
      Only add facts you've checked, and say so where something isn't known.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
